// P3.6 / PS15.1, 15.3–15.7, 15.10: the Hole dialog on an 80 × 50 × 20 plate with three sketch
// points on its top (the geometry asserted in `cadrs_core/tests/applied.rs`: the counterbore's
// closed form, start plane, Up to next, the tapped drill; the tables in `cadrs_core::hole`).
// 01 PS15.1 Hole (the toolbar), the three points picked ("Vertex of Sketch 2"): Metric, Simple,
//    Drilled 5 mm, Start from part, Blind 10 mm with the 118° point; the title is the live callout
//    "Ø 5 mm ↧ 10 mm".
// 02 PS15.4–15.5 Counterbore, Clearance, M5, Close: Ø 5.3 mm, the counterbore Ø 9.75 × 5 from the
//    ISO table; Through all: "Ø 5.3 mm THRU | ⌴Ø 9.75 mm ↧ 5 mm".
// 03 Countersink: Ø 11.2 × 90° ("⌵").
// 04 Tapped M10 (pitch M10x1.5): tap drill Ø 8.5, tapped depth; "M10x1.50 ↧ 10 mm".
// 05 the Pitch list of M10: M10x1.5, M10x1.25, M10x1.
// 06 the Inch tab: ANSI sizes, #10 Clearance (the fit stays Close): Ø 0.196 in (ASME B18.2.8);
//    the callout and the depths in inches (10 mm → 0.394 in).
// 07 PS15.7 Up to next, then accepted: the feature-list row reads the callout (PS15.10).
// 08 PS15.1 a second 40 × 50 × 20 block beside the plate and Sketch 4 with three points (two
//    over the plate, one over the block): Sketch 4 picked in the feature list places a hole at
//    each of its points ("Sketch 4" in the list), each marked with the picked point's amber dot
//    (P3.11, P3.6 judge). PS15.3 (P3.10, the P3.8 judge): the Merge
//    scope defaults to the part the first hole drills, the plate, so the block stays whole
//    (asserted in `hole_whole_sketch_merge_scope_and_parent_below`).
// 09 the block added to the Merge scope: its hole is cut too.
Scenario(
    start: Some("document"),
    steps: [
        WaitFor("document-shell"),
        Wait(30),
        Custom("sketch top rect 0 0 80 50"),
        Wait(5),
        Key("P"),
        Wait(3),
        Key("Shift+7"),
        Wait(40),
        Key("Shift+E"),
        WaitFor("extrude-dialog"),
        Wait(3),
        Click(xyz(40, 25, 0)),
